        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set deconstructs the subject of Stoicism, moving beyond a simple historical overview. It is designed to directly address your questions about its three main figures—Epictetus, Seneca, and Marcus Aurelius—by focusing on *how* their unique life experiences shaped their philosophies. The topics then bridge this historical context to modern-day relevance, investigating the psychological mechanisms that make Stoic principles effective. These avenues of inquiry explore Stoicism's power as a tool for daily life, a shield against cognitive biases, and a direct precursor to contemporary psychological theories like metacognition and self-regulation.",
